Third-party components

The MIT license above covers LCEStudio's own source code. This repository also
bundles or builds on third-party components that are NOT covered by it and
retain their own licenses/terms:

  * lce/converter/  — a vendored cross-platform LCE converter engine, built on
    dtentiion/LCE-Save-Converter. Credit belongs to its authors; its id tables
    are Minecraft's own numbering (data only), and its STFS console-signing
    constants derive from the Horizon project.
  * lce/converter/xcompress64.dll — Microsoft XCompress (XMemCompress/LZX).
  * lce/converter/chm_lzx.dll     — CHMLib LZX decoder.
  * lce/converter/LZXDecompression.dll — LDI (LZX) decoder.
  * lce/lzxc.exe — an external LZX encoder used for console-exact compression.

These binaries are the property of their respective owners and are included
for interoperability only. Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang / Microsoft;
this project is an unofficial, fan-made tool and is not affiliated with or
endorsed by them.
